## v1.0.0b2
+ Add selective impress/submit by object names. In the shell, `impress a b` operates only on the named sub-objects while the no-argument form continues to process all sub-objects collectively. `submit` accepts an optional `--runner <name>` flag and any remaining positional arguments as object names, e.g. `submit --runner cern a b` or `submit a b`.
+ Add `--reference <algorithm>` option to the shell `workaround` command. It copies the referenced algorithm into a `reference/` subdirectory of the workaround space for side-by-side code inspection.
+ Add filelist manifest for the workaround workflow. `workaround_preshell` records the initial algorithm files to `filelist.yaml`, and `workaround_postshell` copies files in the manifest to origin while deleting files in origin that are not listed.
+ Add LHCb Analysis Productions (AP) data list task type (`lhcb_ap_datalist`).
  - `create-lhcb-ap-list` command creates the task with example AP configuration.
  - `add-apd-token` command stores the APD token in `.celebi/config.local.json`.
  - `ls` shows `temp_apd_token` status for these tasks.
+ Deposit uploads `.celebi/config.local.json` alongside the impression so Yuki can generate `lbapi_key.json` server-side.
+ Mark `datalist` and `lhcb_ap_datalist` tasks as validated without requiring an algorithm.
+ Add runner management utilities.
  - `update-runner <name>` command to modify runner settings (URL, token, backend type, Kerberos, EOS mount point).
  - `runners` command now displays full runner configuration.
+ Fix arc cache invalidation so `add-algorithm`/`remove-input` changes are visible immediately in `ls`.
+ Add unit test for arc cache invalidation.
+ Bump version to 1.0.0b2.
+ Fix `book-reana` streaming error message so a connection lost mid-upload is reported as "Connection to Yuki server ... was lost" instead of "Could not connect to Yuki server".
+ Add unit tests for streaming connection-loss scenarios (initial failure vs. mid-stream drop).
+ Refactor `CelebiChrono/interface/shell_modules/reana_booking.py` to reduce complexity and improve maintainability.
+ Resolve all remaining non-informational pylint warnings across `CelebiChrono`, bringing the full-project pylint score to 10.00/10.
+ Fix `status` display to use `status_musical` and `status_legacy` fields from the Yuki server, showing `[coda][finished]` for completed workflows instead of `[coda][coda]`.

## v1.0.0b1
+ Initial beta release of CelebiChrono.
